Z||000000||Formula4ever||07-08-2000||11:19 PM||||I,m putting a 3.4 in my Formula and was wondering if I should use the harmonic balancer from the 3.4 or the 2.8. The 3.4 is from a '95 Camaro it has 25k miles, got it for $700, sound like a good deal? Also, the fuel lines that have the rubber part on them are pretty crusty (rusted). Were can I get new ones? Hay, this place rocks! Cliff you rule!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||07-08-2000||11:27 PM||||You can use the Harmonic balancer only if it's an 88 2.8L. The 88 2.8L and all 3.1L/3.4L are internally balanced.  You will also need the flywheel and flex plate too.<BR>Don't use HB, Fly wheel or flexplate from 87 or earlier engines.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
